course: dictionary
lesson: 1082
title: A boyfriend is a special kind of friend
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A boyfriend is a boy or man that someone is in a romantic relationship with. It means two people like each other more than friends, and it is a private part of their lives.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Asking someone about their boyfriend or girlfriend as a dare is rude.» Rude and private lives tell you that a boyfriend belongs to someone's personal life, not to a joke or a game.
explain: Look at the little words in front of it: «her boyfriend», «his boyfriend», «my boyfriend», «my ex-boyfriend». The word ex- means no longer, so an ex-boyfriend was a boyfriend in the past.
fact: A boyfriend is a boy or man in a romantic relationship with someone. A girlfriend is the girl version of the same idea.
fact: Phrases you may read are her boyfriend, his boyfriend, my boyfriend and ex-boyfriend.
fact: Families can look different. Some children have two mums, two dads, or a mum with a girlfriend or a dad with a boyfriend.
fact: Greet every grown-up in the same polite way, «Hi, nice to meet you», whatever their family looks like.
fact: Teasing a friend that they are your boyfriend is not funny if it upsets them. A parent or teacher can help.
exercise: Which word means a boy or man that someone is in a romantic relationship with? | neighbour | bodyguard | *boyfriend | playmate
exercise: In «my ex-boyfriend», which part tells you he is no longer her boyfriend? | friend | boy | *ex- | my
exercise: If teasing about a boyfriend upsets you, who can help? | Keep it secret forever | *A parent or teacher | The boyfriend himself, alone | Nobody, it is always your fault
test: Which word is the girl version of boyfriend? | girlish | *girlfriend | goodfriend | girlhood
test: «Some children have two mums, two dads.» What should you say when you meet each grown-up? | Go away | *Hi, nice to meet you | Are you dating? | Whisper and walk off
exam: What does the word boyfriend mean? | A boy who plays football for a team | A grown-up who looks after children | A boy who lives next door | *A boy or man someone is in a romantic relationship with
